  # What does this PR do?

  Replaces the simple dialoguer menu with a rich TUI for browsing goals. Users can now navigate
  between local and global goals in separate panels, preview prompt.yaml content before selection,
  and enjoy a polished terminal interface with an ASCII art logo and vim-style keybindings.

  ## Details

  - Added new goal_browser.rs module with dual-panel layout separating local and global goals
  - Implemented view mode allowing users to preview full prompt.yaml content before selection
  - Added ASCII art "Claw" logo rendered in orange and green colors
  - Integrated vim-style navigation (hjkl) alongside arrow keys for all movements
  - Added ratatui and crossterm dependencies for TUI rendering
  - Bumped version from 0.1.0 to 0.2.0
  - Created comprehensive specification document with implementation primer for future LLM-assisted
  development
  - Added 200+ lines of unit tests covering state management and navigation logic

  ## Highlights
```
  /// Entry point for the goal browser TUI.
  pub fn run_goal_browser(goals: Vec<DiscoveredGoal>) -> Result<String> {
      // Set up terminal with alternate screen
      enable_raw_mode().context("Failed to enable raw mode")?;
      let mut stdout = io::stdout();
      execute!(stdout, EnterAlternateScreen)?;

      // Run event loop with dual-panel rendering
      let result = run_app(&mut terminal, &mut app);

      // Clean up terminal state
      disable_raw_mode()?;
      execute!(terminal.backend_mut(), LeaveAlternateScreen)?;

      result
  }
```
  The new browser features:
  - Tab to switch between panels
  - j/k or ↑/↓ to navigate
  - v to preview goal content
  - Enter to select
  - Esc/q to quit

